# This app links React Native and its native modules through SwiftPM, not
# CocoaPods. @react-native-community/cli 20.x only detects an iOS project when a
# Podfile exists, and `react-native spm sync` reads project.ios.sourceDir from
# that CLI config, so this file has to exist. Do not run `pod install`.
raise 'TfliteExample uses SwiftPM. Build the Xcode project directly; do not run pod install.'
